JD 1

Responsibilities:

- Perform hydrologic and hydraulic (H&H) modeling and design calculations for stormwater management, watershed studies, and floodplain delineations.
- Prepare drainage reports, stormwater management plans, and erosion and sediment control (ESC) plans in compliance with local, state, and federal regulations.
- Design stormwater conveyance systems, detention/retention basins, culverts, storm sewers, outfalls, and green stormwater infrastructure (GSI/LID).
- Assist with the preparation and submittal of permit applications to regulatory agencies, including FEMA (LOMR, CLOMR), USACE (Section 404), and state environmental protection departments (NPDES MS4).
- Develop engineering construction plans, specifications, and cost estimates (PS&E) using AutoCAD Civil 3D.
- Perform site visits and field investigations to collect data and assess drainage conditions.
- Review work performed by junior engineers and CAD technicians to ensure technical accuracy and quality control.

Required Qualifications:

- Bachelor of Science degree in Civil Engineering, Environmental Engineering, or Biological Systems Engineering from an ABET-accredited program.
- Engineer-in-Training (EIT) certification required; Professional Engineer (PE) license preferred or on track to obtain within 1 year.
- 3+ years of progressive engineering experience in water resources and stormwater design.
- Working knowledge of local drainage design manuals and stormwater regulatory requirements.

Technical Skills:

- Proficiency in H&H software: HEC-RAS (1D and 2D), HEC-HMS, EPA-SWMM / PCSWMM, HydroCAD, and HY-8.
- Strong proficiency in AutoCAD Civil 3D (Pipe Networks, Surface Creation, Grading).
- Working knowledge of ArcGIS / ArcGIS Pro for spatial data processing and watershed delineation.
- Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Excel, Word, PowerPoint) and Mathcad.

