JD 2

Responsibilities:

- Lead the hydrologic analysis and hydraulic design for transportation and linear infrastructure drainage projects (DOT roadways, bridges, and rail).
- Calculate gutter spread, inlet spacing, cross-drain sizing, bridge hydraulic openings, and scour evaluations in accordance with FHWA and state DOT guidelines.
- Design open and closed drainage systems, roadside ditches, energy dissipators, detention ponds, and stormwater quality features.
- Prepare drainage design documentation, Drainage Design Reports (DDR), Location Hydraulic Studies, and Bridge Hydraulics Reports.
- Coordinate subsurface utility engineering (SUE) and identify/resolve utility conflicts with proposed drainage networks.
- Interface and coordinate with roadway engineers, structural engineers, geotechnical engineers, and environmental specialists.
- Prepare quantities, construction cost estimates, and technical special provisions.

Required Qualifications:

- B.S. in Civil Engineering (Water Resources / Transportation focus preferred).
- Active Professional Engineer (PE) registration or ability to obtain via reciprocity.
- 4+ years of relevant experience specifically focused on roadway and highway drainage design.
- Strong familiarity with FHWA design manuals (HEC-18, HEC-20, HEC-22, HDS-5) and state DOT drainage criteria.

Technical Skills:

- Bentley OpenRoads Designer (Subsurface Utilities Design and Analysis - SUDA) and/or AutoCAD Civil 3D.
- StormCAD, CivilStorm, Bentley FlowMaster, CulvertMaster, and HY-8.
- MicroStation V8i / CONNECT Edition.
- HEC-RAS for bridge hydraulic modeling and riverine analysis.

