- B.S. in Civil Engineering.
- Fundamentals of Engineering (FE) / Engineer-in-Training (EIT) certification required.
- 2–5 years of site civil engineering and stormwater management design experience.
- Understanding of local municipal codes, zoning bylaws, and clean water regulations.

Technical Skills:

- AutoCAD Civil 3D (including surfaces, alignments, profiles, and pipe networks).
- HydroCAD, Hydraflow Hydrographs / Storm Sewers, or SSA (Storm and Sanitary Analysis).
- Bluebeam Revu and Adobe Acrobat for redline markups and submittal reviews.
- Microsoft Excel for custom hydraulic calculation spreadsheets.

