- 2–5 years of applied experience in numerical hydrologic modeling and environmental data science.
- Deep knowledge of statistical hydrology, extreme value theory, and physical watershed processes.

Technical Skills:

- HEC-HMS, SWAT (Soil & Water Assessment Tool), VIC (Variable Infiltration Capacity), or PRMS.
- Advanced programming skills in Python (Pandas, GeoPandas, Xarray, SciPy, Hydrostats) or R (hydroTSM, lfstat).
- Cloud geospatial analysis (Google Earth Engine, AWS S3 geospatial datasets).
- ArcGIS Pro / QGIS and HEC-SSP (Statistical Software Package).

